# Core Implementation

## Module Breakdown

Split the implementation across these modules. Only create a module when its concern is present:

| File | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `src/main.c` | Entry point only — parse args, dispatch, call `output_loop()` |
| `src/args.c` / `src/args.h` | Argument parsing, flag detection (`--help`, `--version`), string joining |
| `src/output.c` / `src/output.h` | Buffered write loop to stdout |
| `src/version.h` | Version string, author, licence constants |

`main.c` must stay thin. It should contain no business logic — only wiring.

