## `src/main.c`

```c
#include "args.h"
#include "output.h"
#include "version.h"
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    Args args;

    if (args_parse(argc, argv, &args) != 0) {
        return EXIT_FAILURE;
    }

    if (args.show_version) {
        printf("yes-toto %s\n", YES_TOTO_VERSION);
        printf("Author:  %s\n", YES_TOTO_AUTHOR);
        printf("License: %s\n", YES_TOTO_LICENSE);
        return EXIT_SUCCESS;
    }

    if (args.show_help) {
        printf("Usage: yes-toto [STRING]...\n");
        printf("       yes-toto [OPTION]\n\n");
        printf("Repeatedly output a line with STRING, or 'y'.\n\n");
        printf("Options:\n");
        printf("  -h, --help     display this help and exit\n");
        printf("  -v, --version  output version information and exit\n");
        return EXIT_SUCCESS;
    }

    output_loop(args.output);
    return EXIT_SUCCESS;
}
```

---

## Exit Behavior

| Situation | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| Broken pipe / stdout closed | `fwrite` returns short → `output_loop` returns → `main` returns `EXIT_SUCCESS` |
| SIGINT (Ctrl+C) | OS delivers signal → process terminates (default handler) |
| Unknown flag | Error message to stderr → `EXIT_FAILURE` |
| `--help` | Usage printed to stdout → `EXIT_SUCCESS` |
| `--version` / `-v` | Version info printed to stdout → `EXIT_SUCCESS` |

---

## What Not to Generate

- ❌ `printf` or `fputs` inside the hot loop — use `fwrite` with a pre-filled buffer
- ❌ `fflush` inside the hot loop
- ❌ `exit()` calls inside modules — only `main` may return an exit code
- ❌ Signal handlers — default OS behavior is correct
- ❌ Dynamic memory allocation (`malloc`/`calloc`) — use stack buffers
- ❌ Global mutable state outside of `main`
- ❌ Recursive functions

